+# Catalog
+
+For whoever changes the item page or enables its cache. Item searches can reuse disposable Redis results to reduce
+repeated queries during the Saturday morning slowdown.
+
+## Search results
+
+[The item query](../../larder/catalog.py) returns matching items in name order. Passing a cache to `items` enables
+caching; existing calls without one continue to query Postgres. The implementation owns the key format, expiry and
+validation. Empty results are cached too. Read errors, malformed entries and write errors are logged and fall back
+to the database result; database errors still propagate.
+
+## Enable the cache
+
+Install the optional client dependency with `python3 -m pip install -r requirements-cache.txt`. At application
+startup, create a client once per web process and pass it to catalog calls:
+
+```python
+import os
+
+from larder.catalog import items, redis_cache
+
+cache = redis_cache(os.environ["REDIS_URL"])
+# At the item query call site, with its existing database connection and search:
+results = items(conn, query, cache=cache)
+```
+
+The repository contains no web entry point to wire this into. Set `REDIS_URL` in the deployment to Tom's Redis
+instance (for example, `redis://127.0.0.1:6379/0` on the same server). Use a separate Redis database for each larder
+deployment: keys assume a single pantry database. The client factory sets 50 ms socket and connection timeouts and
+disables retries, following the [Redis client timeout controls](https://redis.io/docs/latest/develop/clients/redis-py/produsage/).
+Remove the `cache` argument to disable caching without requiring Redis to be available.
+
+## Known limits
+
+- Results include stock and can be stale for the ten-second expiry after a query completes. Reads do not renew the
+  expiry. Bypass the cache with `items(conn, query)` wherever current stock is required; cached stock is unsuitable
+  for reserving or confirming an order.
+- Simultaneous misses can each query Postgres. Check query timings and database load under Saturday traffic before
+  treating caching as a confirmed performance fix.
+- Redis failures restore query load and may add cache socket waits. Check cache warnings and Redis availability;
+  disable caching if those waits worsen response times.
+
+## Shaped by
+
+- [Use Redis for disposable catalog results](../adr/0003-use-redis-for-disposable-catalog-results.md).
